
FLASHING

1. Refer to the documentation here: https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/latest/esp32/get-started/index.html to setup esp-idf on any OS.
2. Modify your/path/to/esp-idf/components/lwip/lwip/src/core:513 to be "if (force || IP_FORWARD) {"
3. Navigate into mcmb/txrx
4. Execute idf.py build
5. Execute idf.py flash


CONFIGURING TX/RX

1. Connect to the wifi
2. If first config, in a web-browser, type "192.168.2.1" into the URL bar, otherwise, type the configured ip
3. Adjust network settings as needed


THEORY OF OPERATION

This project uses ip4 networking fundamentals to acheive modbus communication using both ethernet and wifi connections. tx and rx both host wifi access points
to allow for interconnection (tx and rx) and configuration (user to device). tx and rx may connect succesfully using any of three methods: tx sta may connect to
rx ap; rx sta may connect to tx ap; tx eth may connect to rx eth. Once tx and rx have established a connection, careful networking may be used to allow tx/rx
to read/write messages to any device that is connected to tx/rx eth/ap/sta (those slashes are correct! all devices connected to tx and rx [including tx and rx]
can be accessed by either device if the configuration is set up properly).



BARE MINIMUM TX/RX CONFIG FOR PROPER FUNCTION

1. tx/rx's eth/ap/sta ip4 must be unique ip4 addresses; likewise dat-8024 ip4 must be unique
2. eth ip4 must be in a different subnet than ap/sta ip4 on tx/rx
3. rx's eth ip4 must be in the same subnet as dat-8024's ip4
4. every netif must have a valid ip4 as it's gw and every netif must have a valid nm
5. tx's sta gw must be set with rx's ap ip4
!!! pay careful attention to the subnets being properly differentiated by each netif's nm !!!
